## Reflection

<details style="margin-top: 12px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden;">
  <summary style="background-color: #E4E2F8; padding: 12px 16px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; color: #1F1976; font-size: 16px;">
    &#128161; Where in the three days will your students need the most time, and what will you do when a class falls behind?
  </summary>
  <div style="background-color: #FFFFFF; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid #ACA8EA; font-size: 16px; color: #1A1A1A; line-height: 1.6;">
    Most classes feel the squeeze on Day 2, when students turn a paper table into Python. The lesson expects most students to finish Level 3 and start Level 4 that day, with the rest carrying into Day 3, so plan for that slack. If a class falls behind earlier, on features during Day 1, resolve it before labeling, because every later step builds on those three questions.
  </div>
</details>

## Share Out

Add one move to the board for your own class: how you'd adjust the three days, or the question you'll ask a student whose features aren't working.

